1
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:03,830
Come on, Joey!

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,380
Rach, I told you everything I knew last night.

3
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:10,300
It's not that big a deal. So Monica and Chandler are doing it.

4
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:13,130
I cannot believe you would say that!

5
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:17,050
Sorry. Monica and Chandler are "making love."

6
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:21,850
No, I mean, come on. This is a huge deal!

7
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:25,060
I need more details. Who initiated the first kiss?

8
00:00:25,690 --> 00:00:27,480
I don't know.

9
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:30,400
Is he romantic with her?

10
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:32,690
I don't know.

11
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:35,200
Are they in love?

12
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,030
- I don't know.     - Ugh.

13
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:40,330
You don't know anything.

14
00:00:40,490 --> 00:00:42,240
- Oh! I know one thing.     - What?

15
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:44,710
They did it right there on the couch.

16
00:01:32,670 --> 00:01:35,080

17
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:38,260
- Hey, Ross.     - Yeah.

18
00:01:38,930 --> 00:01:41,220
Gunther, could I have a scone, please?

19
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:42,970
Want to hear some good news?

20
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:44,770
Someone I know is getting married.

21
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:48,980
Yeah, weddings are happy occasions. Oh, by the by, it's my ex-wife, Emily!

22
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:51,980
Sorry, man.

23
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:54,860
- Here's your scone.     - Thanks, Gunther.

24
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,440
Thanks.

25
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:59,530
Stupid British snack food!

26
00:02:01,320 --> 00:02:03,870
Did they teach you that in anger management?

27
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:08,370
You know what might help deal with it? Think of it this way.

28
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:12,000
You and Emily are in the past. You can't be mad about the past.

29
00:02:12,170 --> 00:02:16,000
Are you still mad about, you know, the Louisiana Purchase?

30
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:22,260
- I don't think anybody's mad about that.     - Exactly! Because it's in the past.

31
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:27,270
Anybody going to eat that?

32
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:35,320
Look at us all dressed up for the party. What are we celebrating?

33
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:38,320
We had a lot of liquor left over from the Christmas party.

34
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:41,570
I think this is cool. None of our friends are here.

35
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:43,990
We can be a real couple. We don't have to hide.

36
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:46,870
- I know. I can do this.     - Ooh.

37
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:48,750
And I can do this.

38
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,290
- We can't do that.     - We can't do that.

39
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:55,790
Hey, Bing! Ha-ha-ha.

40
00:02:56,460 --> 00:03:00,010
Whoa! Who's the pretty lady, and what is she doing with you?

41
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:03,840
Ha-ha-ha! I ask myself that very question. This is Monica.

42
00:03:04,010 --> 00:03:06,850
- My boss, Doug. This is Monica.     - Hi, nice to meet you.

43
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:09,640
- Hi! This is my wife, Kara.     - Nice to meet you.

44
00:03:09,810 --> 00:03:11,140
- Bing!     - Okay!

45
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,980
Did you hear about the new law firm working for us?

46
00:03:15,150 --> 00:03:17,020
- No, sir.     - Yeah, Dewey, Cheatem & Howe.

47
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:23,450
Come on, let's go drink our body weight.

48
00:03:25,950 --> 00:03:27,370
- What was that?      - What?

49
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:28,700
That noise you made?

50
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:31,870
- Oh, that was my work laugh.     - Your work laugh?

51
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:36,000
If you're going to survive this party, you have to come up with one too.

52
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:39,420
- All right. Check me out.     - Okay.

53
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:42,470
He says, "$30, Father. Same as in town." Ha!

54
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:52,520
Hey, everybody at work loved you last night.

55
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:54,230
- Really?     - And they like me more...

56
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,940
...just because I was with you.

57
00:03:56,110 --> 00:03:59,110
You repaired a lot of the damage from when they met Joey.

58
00:04:00,940 --> 00:04:04,450
Doug wants us to play tennis. He's never talked to me outside of work.

59
00:04:04,610 --> 00:04:07,030
Except for that time at that strip club.

60
00:04:09,450 --> 00:04:11,040
Strip church.

61
00:04:13,210 --> 00:04:16,040
- I'm gonna go try to find a racket.     - I thought you had one.

62
00:04:16,210 --> 00:04:20,300
I used to, but then Joey thought it'd be fun to go to Central Park and hit rocks...

63
00:04:20,550 --> 00:04:22,210
...at bigger rocks.

64
00:04:23,090 --> 00:04:25,430
- Hey, Rach, do you have a tennis racket?     - Hey.

65
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:28,390
Oh, um, I lent it to Joey and I've never gotten it back.

66
00:04:29,470 --> 00:04:30,680
Okay, good luck with that.

67
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:35,020
- Ahem. Hey.     - Hey.

68
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:36,400
What's up?

69
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:39,270
What are you doing here? I thought you had inventory.

70
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,860
Well I do, but I decided I'd take a long lunch...

71
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:44,610
...and spend some time with my friend, Monica.

72
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:48,450
You know, I feel like we don't talk anymore.

73
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:50,120
How are you?

74
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:51,790
What is new with you?

75
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:55,160
Heh, um...

76
00:04:55,330 --> 00:04:57,620
Not much. Um, work's good.

77
00:04:57,790 --> 00:05:00,920
We don't have to talk about work. We could talk about anything.

78
00:05:02,050 --> 00:05:03,590
Okay. Um...

79
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,550
Hey! You know what?

80
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:07,930
Let's talk about relationships.

81
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:11,140
- Okay. What's going on with you?     - Nothing.

82
00:05:12,390 --> 00:05:13,810
You go.

83
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:17,390
Well, I... There was this guy at the bank that I thought was cute.

84
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:19,600
Um, but I don't anymore.

85
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:23,690
Wow, that's, uh, juicy. Ahem, um...

86
00:05:23,860 --> 00:05:27,150
You know what? I actually do have a lot of work to do.

87
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:30,740
You're sure there's just not anything else?

88
00:05:30,910 --> 00:05:34,490
Yes, I'm sure. Is there something you want to talk to me about?

89
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:35,910
No.

90
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:40,290
I...

91
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:42,500
If there was, I wouldn't tell you.

92
00:05:50,430 --> 00:05:51,760
Okay, then what happened?

93
00:05:52,510 --> 00:05:55,020
Uh, oh! Aw.

94
00:05:55,180 --> 00:05:56,560
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

95
00:05:57,980 --> 00:05:59,900
Ah-ah, you'll get your turn.

96
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,900
- Hey, Pheebs. What's going on?     - Hey. Nothing.

97
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,440
This is not over.

98
00:06:05,610 --> 00:06:07,690
- No, no, no!     - What?

99
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:11,240
Ugh, I was up all night writing this really nasty letter to Emily.

100
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:14,370
It was perfect, and now it's all covered in...

101
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,240
Actually, thanks!

102
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:19,080
All right! Everybody ready to go to the movies?

103
00:06:19,250 --> 00:06:22,170
Uh, actually, I think I'm gonna skip it.

104
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,630
- Really?     - I'm gonna stay and read my book.

105
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,590
I just want to be alone right now.

106
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:28,340
Oh. Sure you don't want to come?

107
00:06:28,510 --> 00:06:32,680
Tom Hanks, Meg Ryan. They get mail and stuff.

108
00:06:34,470 --> 00:06:35,890
- That's okay, Joe.     - All right.

109
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:37,680
Let's go, Pheebs.

110
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,100
Oh, God!

111
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:48,440
Bing!

112
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:53,070
- Unh!     - Aah!

113
00:06:53,570 --> 00:06:54,870
Game!

114
00:06:56,660 --> 00:07:00,210
Yeah, I gotta tell you, that partner of yours is a real tiger.

115
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:03,170
Are you all right?

116
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:07,880
We'll just get a little sip of water.

117
00:07:09,670 --> 00:07:12,380
Am I on fire today or what?

118
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:16,720
Those birds are browned, basted and ready to be carved.

119
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:19,390
Okay, easy, Martina.

120
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,690
I think we should let them win the next game.

121
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:26,860
I'm sorry, I don't understand what you just said.

122
00:07:28,190 --> 00:07:29,230
Let them win one.

123
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:33,660
Are you crazy? We own those two. Look at them!

124
00:07:33,990 --> 00:07:36,950
He can't even breathe, and she's popping pills.

125
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,740
You're not giving them a chance.

126
00:07:39,950 --> 00:07:41,460
They have rackets, don't they?

127
00:07:43,580 --> 00:07:46,750
Uh, Bing, I think we're gonna make this the last game.

128
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,960
Yes, sir. Put me out of my misery.

129
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:51,720
Are you sure you never played pro? Ha-ha-ha.

130
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,090
Please let them win.

131
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:56,970
I'll take it down to 95 percent, but that's the best I can do.

132
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,640
- Oopsie! Missed it!     - I got it!

133
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:09,520
Nice shot.

134
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,540
I got it!

135
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:23,120
Long!

136
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,460
I can't believe you let them win.

137
00:08:31,630 --> 00:08:34,930
Yeah, well, at least you hid your feelings well about it.

138
00:08:35,590 --> 00:08:37,890
- I was frustrated.     - It was my racket.

139
00:08:38,050 --> 00:08:39,350
I was frustrated with you!

140
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:44,140
If we hadn't lost, they would never have invited us to dinner tomorrow.

141
00:08:44,350 --> 00:08:45,480
What bothers me...

142
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:48,060
...is how different you act around them.

143
00:08:48,310 --> 00:08:51,190
The throwing the tennis games, the fake laugh...

144
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:54,240
...the "See you later, Bing!" "Not if I see you first, Doug!"

145
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:00,660
I don't like "work Chandler." The guy's a suck-up.

146
00:09:01,410 --> 00:09:03,290
You know what? Because you said that...

147
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:05,370
...I'm not putting out tonight!

148
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,880
Something's wrong. My brother does not stay out all night.

149
00:09:16,050 --> 00:09:18,180
Maybe we should check the trash chute.

150
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:22,140
Ross couldn't fit down the trash chute.

151
00:09:22,350 --> 00:09:24,600
That's right. He almost could.

152
00:09:24,850 --> 00:09:27,310
Which is exactly how I got stuck there.

153
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:30,360
- Hey!     - Hey.

154
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,070
Oh, my God!

155
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,440
Where the hell have you been?

156
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:37,530
Just, you know, out.

157
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:42,280
Oh, out! God, I don't know why we didn't think to check there.

158
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:43,990
What were you doing?

159
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:47,000
I, uh, went to a bar and then...

160
00:09:47,250 --> 00:09:50,630
...I just, uh, walked around for a while.

161
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:54,050
You walked around all night in the city by yourself?

162
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,090
He hooked up!

163
00:09:59,050 --> 00:10:00,390
He hooked up with someone.

164
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:03,810
I don't have to answer your questions. Okay? I'm a big boy.

165
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,350
I can do whatever I want.

166
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:06,810
He hooked up!

167
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:11,060
Tell us about her!

168
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:13,400
Ross, you left your scarf...

169
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:22,450
Hey, you guys.

170
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:33,080
Okay. Okay.

171
00:10:33,250 --> 00:10:37,170
I know what you all are thinking, but Chandler is in Yemen.

172
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:42,220
I'm a young woman. I have needs. I can't wait forever.

173
00:10:42,390 --> 00:10:44,470
Yeah, no, that's what I was thinking.

174
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:50,850
So I'm asking you, please just take a moment before you judge me.

175
00:10:51,020 --> 00:10:52,350
Oh, nobody's judging you.

176
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,690
Oh.

177
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:58,360
Okay, you, Mr. Right-place-at-the-right-time...

178
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:01,700
...call me.

179
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:13,000
Okay, look, I know what you guys are going to say.

180
00:11:13,210 --> 00:11:15,840
You two would have very hairy children.

181
00:11:17,590 --> 00:11:19,420
I didn't know you'd say that.

182
00:11:20,510 --> 00:11:22,470
Ross! Janice?

183
00:11:22,680 --> 00:11:24,590
All right. Hold on, hold on, hold on.

184
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:26,640
This is Ross. Okay?

185
00:11:26,850 --> 00:11:30,020
He's our friend. He obviously went crazy.

186
00:11:30,230 --> 00:11:32,230
He obviously lost his mind.

187
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:36,730
I didn't lose my mind, okay? Janice and I have a lot in common.

188
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:41,110
We've both been divorced. We both have kids.

189
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:43,240
Are you going to see her again?

190
00:11:43,450 --> 00:11:46,240
- Don't put ideas in his head!     - I am gonna see her again.

191
00:11:46,450 --> 00:11:48,490
Damn it, Phoebe!

192
00:11:52,790 --> 00:11:55,960
I have to tell you something that I've never admitted.

193
00:11:56,130 --> 00:12:00,340
In high school, I made out with James even though I knew that you liked him.

194
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:03,800
Wow! That feels so good to get off my chest. Okay, you go.

195
00:12:05,340 --> 00:12:07,890
- My turn? What are you talking about?     - Ugh.

196
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,350
Monica...

197
00:12:10,350 --> 00:12:12,310
I know about you and Chandler.

198
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,480
What?

199
00:12:14,650 --> 00:12:17,020
I overheard you on the phone the other day.

200
00:12:17,190 --> 00:12:21,530
You said, "I'll tell Rachel I'm doing laundry for a couple of hours."

201
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:24,780
And he said, "Laundry? Is that my new nickname?"

202
00:12:24,950 --> 00:12:26,870
And you said, "No.

203
00:12:27,030 --> 00:12:31,040
You know what your nickname is, Mr. Big."

204
00:12:35,170 --> 00:12:36,580
Well, heh...

205
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:39,590
Sounds like you're writing yourself a little play there, Rach.

206
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:44,300
Wow, I... Let me know how that one turns out.

207
00:12:44,470 --> 00:12:48,970
I wouldn't know because I got so freaked out I hung up the phone.

208
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:51,600
Well, if you had kept listening, ha-ha-ha...

209
00:12:51,850 --> 00:12:55,560
...you would have heard me call him Mister Big...

210
00:12:55,730 --> 00:12:57,650
...ot.     - What?

211
00:12:57,810 --> 00:12:59,610
Mr. Bigot.

212
00:13:00,730 --> 00:13:04,570
Ha, ha. He tells the most racist jokes.

213
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:08,070
All right. So that's it.

214
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:11,950
You're telling me there's nothing going on between you and Chandler?

215
00:13:12,290 --> 00:13:14,160
Me and Chandler?

216
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:20,540
- Put your $20 down.     - Okay.

217
00:13:20,710 --> 00:13:22,960
First one to find the tasty treat wins.

218
00:13:23,130 --> 00:13:24,840
- Okay? All right.     - Mm-hm.

219
00:13:25,010 --> 00:13:28,260
Let's get the contestants out of their isolation booths.

220
00:13:29,390 --> 00:13:30,850
And they're off!

221
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:32,430
Whoa.

222
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:34,770
Get your foot off my contestant! Judge?

223
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,940
Judge rules no violation.

224
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:38,190
Agh.

225
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:40,940
- Hey, guys.     - Yeah.

226
00:13:42,110 --> 00:13:46,320
It's so weird to say this, but I just had a great date with Janice.

227
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:48,070
- What?     - Are you serious?

228
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:52,910
Yeah. I opened up to her about all the terrible stuff that's been happening to me.

229
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,200
I mean, I talked for hours.

230
00:13:55,370 --> 00:13:56,500
It is amazing...

231
00:13:56,710 --> 00:14:00,290
...to have someone give you such focused attention.

232
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:03,460
You don't need Janice for that. You've got us.

233
00:14:03,630 --> 00:14:06,710
- And the duck gets the Nutter Butter!     - No! Agh!

234
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:09,590
That's not a Nutter Butter. That's an old won ton!

235
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:11,090
Judge rules...

236
00:14:11,390 --> 00:14:13,390
...Nutter Butter.     - Ugh.

237
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:15,060
- Tough call.     - Yeah.

238
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:24,020
Seriously, I strongly believe that we should all support President Clinton...

239
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:25,530
...and her husband, Bill.

240
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:31,030
So how do you like your coffee?

241
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:33,240
- None for me.      - Just a little bit of sugar.

242
00:14:33,410 --> 00:14:35,450
I'll have Monica stick her finger in it.

243
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:37,000
That ought to sweeten it up.

244
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:44,460
- How does that not give you a headache?     - You get used to it.

245
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:46,130
I don't think that I can.

246
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:48,800
Maybe this will be it for me on the work things.

247
00:14:48,970 --> 00:14:51,430
So I laugh at my boss's jokes. What's the big deal?

248
00:14:51,590 --> 00:14:54,140
I'd rather not hang out with this work-weasel guy...

249
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:57,640
...when I could be with my boyfriend, who I actually respect.

250
00:14:57,810 --> 00:14:59,140
Oh.

251
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:01,850
Ah, heh.

252
00:15:02,020 --> 00:15:04,310
I gotta apologize for Kara's coffee.

253
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:06,480
I'd feel sorry for it if it got in a fight.

254
00:15:06,650 --> 00:15:10,530
It's not strong enough to defend itself. Ha-ha-ha!

255
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:14,910
Hear what I said?

256
00:15:15,910 --> 00:15:17,080
What?

257
00:15:18,040 --> 00:15:20,410
It's a joke, Bing. What's the matter with you?

258
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:23,670
Well, I just didn't think it was funny, sir.

259
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:24,920
Excuse me?

260
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:28,380
- Well, I just...     - Honey?

261
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:31,090
I just don't think you understood the joke.

262
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:33,720
- Really?      - Yeah.

263
00:15:33,890 --> 00:15:37,310
I mean, it was really funny. I just don't think that you got it.

264
00:15:37,470 --> 00:15:41,060
Heh, you see, Kara's coffee is weak-tasting.

265
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:45,190
But what Doug did was imply that it was weak physically.

266
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,610
- You get it now, honey?      - I think I do!

267
00:15:54,570 --> 00:15:57,080
- Thank you, Monica.     - I thought you could use the help.

268
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,830
Ha-ha-ha.

269
00:15:58,990 --> 00:16:00,410
Coffee in a fight!

270
00:16:05,210 --> 00:16:06,380
Hey, Rach.

271
00:16:06,540 --> 00:16:09,050
You mind if I read my comic books in here?

272
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:13,630
Sure. Why?

273
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:17,800
Chandler and Monica are over there. It's kind of hard to concentrate.

274
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:22,430
What? She just called and said she was going to be working late.

275
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,390
She keeps lying to me.

276
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:28,650
That's it! I'm gonna go over there and I'm confronting them right now.

277
00:16:39,370 --> 00:16:43,450
So you're telling me that I have to tell racist jokes now?

278
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:46,500
I'm just not very good at this.

279
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:49,590
I'm a terrible liar. I hate having to lie to Rachel.

280
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:52,550
- But we're not ready to tell yet.      - I know.

281
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:57,470
Ever since high school, Rachel was the one person that I told everything to.

282
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:59,890
I miss that so much now.

283
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:02,430
She's my best friend.

284
00:17:09,110 --> 00:17:10,270
Joey?

285
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,980
- Oh, my God, Rachel!     - Hey!

286
00:17:13,150 --> 00:17:14,860
Hi!

287
00:17:16,450 --> 00:17:18,360
What are you doing here?

288
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:23,950
Well, I actually came over here to borrow this lamp...

289
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:26,710
...to, um, look at my books.

290
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,960
You know, see them a little better. Heh.

291
00:17:30,590 --> 00:17:33,590
- Okay, great. Great. Um...      - Yeah.

292
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:37,300
Well, what I was doing in Chandler's room is that, um...

293
00:17:37,550 --> 00:17:38,840
...I was cleaning it.

294
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:42,810
- In fact, he pays me to clean it.      - Oh!

295
00:17:42,970 --> 00:17:46,430
What a great way to make some extra pocket money.

296
00:17:47,770 --> 00:17:51,020
When I said to you earlier that I was at work, um...

297
00:17:51,230 --> 00:17:52,940
...I'm at my new work.

298
00:17:53,570 --> 00:17:55,900
Good enough. Right?

299
00:17:57,110 --> 00:17:59,030
Okay, well, um...

300
00:17:59,660 --> 00:18:01,320
I'm gonna go look at my books.

301
00:18:02,530 --> 00:18:05,830
- Okay. Go get back to my new job.     - Okay.

302
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:08,790
Okay.

303
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:14,340
Congratulations on your new job!

304
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:22,890
Man, she is really gullible.

305
00:18:26,890 --> 00:18:29,470

306
00:18:29,690 --> 00:18:31,810
- Here you go.     - Thanks.

307
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:34,610
- Actually, I should get going.      - You're sure?

308
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:37,070
I can stay out as late as you want.

309
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:39,360
I told you I'm on sabbatical from work...

310
00:18:39,570 --> 00:18:42,530
Yes, yes. You did. Ha-ha-ha.

311
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:45,080
- Oh, man!     - What is wrong now?

312
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:48,160
This isn't what I ordered.

313
00:18:48,370 --> 00:18:52,540
Man! Can't anything go right in my life?

314
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:56,250
First, my marriage falls apart, and then...

315
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:57,590
I know, I know!

316
00:18:57,800 --> 00:19:00,550
You lose your apartment, then you lose your job...

317
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:03,760
...then your ex-wife gets married so fast! And now the coffee!

318
00:19:03,930 --> 00:19:05,510
Aah!

319
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:07,390
Ross...

320
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:10,310
...we need to talk.     - Okay.

321
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:13,730
- Sometimes I feel...     - No, no, don't.

322
00:19:13,940 --> 00:19:15,900
I'm going to talk.

323
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:18,230
I believe...

324
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:21,320
...that the sun has set...

325
00:19:21,530 --> 00:19:24,780
...on our day in the sun.

326
00:19:25,990 --> 00:19:30,710
- What?     - You're a very sweet person, Ross.

327
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:32,750
Um...

328
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:34,710
Unfortunately...

329
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:39,090
...I just don't think I can take another second of you whining!

330
00:19:42,050 --> 00:19:45,510
Let me make sure I'm hearing this right.

331
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:50,140
You're ending this with me because...

332
00:19:50,390 --> 00:19:51,930
...I'm too whiny?

333
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,440
Mm.

334
00:19:55,310 --> 00:19:57,110
So you're saying...

335
00:19:57,360 --> 00:20:00,530
...I've become so whiny...

336
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:02,450
...that I...

337
00:20:02,650 --> 00:20:05,320
...annoy you...

338
00:20:06,530 --> 00:20:08,160
...Janice.

339
00:20:08,490 --> 00:20:09,740
Well, yeah!

340
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,540
Oh, my God!

341
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:18,710
- Are you gonna be okay?     - I am now.

342
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:20,300
Okay.

343
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:27,300
- Hi.     - Oh, hi.

344
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,760
Well...

345
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,640
I guess, that's two out of three...

346
00:20:33,770 --> 00:20:34,810
...Joey!

347
00:20:45,660 --> 00:20:48,740
- Dude, we gotta talk.     - Okay.

348
00:20:48,910 --> 00:20:52,700
I want to tell you something before you heard it from someone else.

349
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:56,370
I hope this isn't too weird but, uh...

350
00:20:57,330 --> 00:20:59,920
...I had a thing with Janice.

351
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:06,220
You're not mad?

352
00:21:06,430 --> 00:21:07,640
Why would I be mad?

353
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:11,060
Because there's certain rules about this kind of stuff.

354
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:15,020
You don't, uh... You don't fool around with your friends' ex-girlfriends...

355
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:16,310
...or, uh...

356
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:19,560
...possible girlfriends or girls they're related to.

357
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:26,570
I am mad.

358
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:30,910
But you know what I'm gonna do? I'm gonna forgive you.

359
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:33,120
Because that's what friends do.

360
00:21:33,290 --> 00:21:36,290
They forgive their friends when they do everything you just said.

361
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:39,000
- All the things on the list there.     - Thank you.

362
00:21:39,250 --> 00:21:40,920
But I want you to remember...

363
00:21:41,130 --> 00:21:43,460
...that I forgave you.

364
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:46,880
- Okay.     - I also want you to remember...

365
00:21:47,050 --> 00:21:49,970
...that I let you live here rent-free.

366
00:21:50,470 --> 00:21:52,850
- All right.     - And I want you to remember...

367
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:57,600
...that I gave you 27 dollars.

368
00:21:58,980 --> 00:22:00,150
No strings attached!

369
00:22:00,310 --> 00:22:01,860
If you can't remember that...

370
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:04,690
...I think we should write it down. Let's write it down!

